     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've flagged this growth stage as anomalous and asked for someone to check. Argon flow has stayed at about 100 sccm, but tube pressure has risen steadily from about 3.02 to 3.48 Torr since the stage began at t=2520 s.\n\n- **Most likely causes:** air leaking in through a bad seal, or a partly blocked exhaust or pump line. Both would push pressure up like this. This furnace has no exhaust O2 sensor, so I can't tell them apart or confirm the growth atmosphere.\n- **What still looks normal:** temperature is holding at 750 °C and heater power is steady.\n- **Sample:** there's no characterization data yet. Whatever grows during this stretch shouldn't count as evidence about the recipe unless the cause is found and cleared.\n\nTo settle it, isolate the tube and see how fast pressure rises (a leak-up test), and inspect the exhaust line and pump."
     }
    ],
